{% comment %}
  Product-specific FAQs — diagnosis-first, no miracle/glow copy.
  Renders details elements for pdp-faq when use_formula_catalog is on.
{% endcomment %}
{% case product.handle %}
  {% when '5-niacinamide-serum-acne-prone-skin' %}
    <details open>
      <summary>What problem is this serum actually for?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Oil dysregulation, visible pores, and uneven tone on acne-prone skin — not “dullness” as a vague claim. If your barrier is badly compromised, repair moisture first, then introduce this treat step slowly.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why 5% encapsulated Niacinamide — not just “with niacinamide”?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Concentration and delivery matter. Encapsulated 5% sits in a stabilised matrix with SEPICONCONTROL™ A5 and Zinc PCA on a second sebum pathway — a dual system most single-active serums skip. <a href="/pages/ingredients#ingredient-niacinamide">Read the ingredient card</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will it clear an active pimple overnight?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>No — and we will not claim that. This serum supports oil balance and clearer-looking texture with consistency. For a single lesion, pair with a targeted step like Clear Seal, or speak with consultation.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I layer it with acids or vitamin C?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Yes, with planning. If your skin is new to actives, alternate nights with strong AHAs/BHAs. Vitamin C often fits morning under SPF; keep this serum in the treat step once or twice daily as tolerated.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I still need moisturiser and SPF?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Yes. Seal with a barrier-aware moisturiser. In the morning, finish with broad-spectrum SPF — especially on Indian UV and pigmentation-prone skin. <a href="/pages/barrier">Barrier literacy</a> · <a href="/pages/daily-spf">Daily SPF</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it contain fragrance?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>No added fragrance. The formula prioritises actives and comfort for acne-prone routines.</p></div>
    </details>

  {% when 'calming-moisturiser-acne-prone-skin' %}
    <details open>
      <summary>Why does cream fail if my barrier is compromised?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Moisturiser cannot replace missing lipids. When the barrier is stressed, TEWL rises and products sting or “don’t absorb.” This formula replenishes ceramides and phospholipids first — then hydration can hold. <a href="/pages/barrier">Read barrier literacy</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will it clog acne-prone pores?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>It is built as a lightweight, under-SPF moisturiser using C15-19 Alkane for cushion without grease. If you are highly congestion-prone, use a thin layer and keep cleanse + treat consistent.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What do the botanicals actually do?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>The six-botanical complex (Amla, Licorice, Tulsi, Black Seed, Neem, Phytic Acid) has named roles for brightening support, antioxidant defence, and anti-acne support — not decorative “natural” marketing. <a href="/pages/ingredients#ingredient-botanical-six">Ingredient card</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Morning, night, or both?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Both. Morning: moisturise then SPF. Night: after serum. If skin is reactive, start once daily.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it contain fragrance?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>No added fragrance. Focus stays on barrier lipids, emollients, and the botanical complex.</p></div>
    </details>

  {% when 'refreshing-cleanser-acne-prone-skin' %}
    <details open>
      <summary>Are my breakouts a cleanliness problem?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Usually not. Congestion and oil dysregulation sit inside a barrier that harsh cleansers often worsen. This cleanser uses functional 2% BHA + 1% AHA with mild surfactants and phospholipids — clear without strip. <a href="/pages/acne">Acne literacy</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why list acid percentages on a rinse-off cleanser?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Because token acid mentions are common. Salicylic Acid at 2% and Glycolic Acid at 1% are functional rinse-off levels with a clear mechanism — oil-soluble inside the pore, water-soluble on the surface.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How often should I use it?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Once or twice daily. If skin feels tight, drop to once daily, moisturise well, and avoid stacking more acids the same night.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I use it with the Niacinamide serum?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Yes — cleanse first, then serum. That is the intended Project Skin sequence. Introduce one change at a time if your barrier is reactive.</p></div>
    </details>

  {% when 'protecting-sunscreen-acne-prone-skin' %}
    <details open>
      <summary>Is SPF seasonal in India?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>No. High UV load is nearly year-round; cloudy days still transmit UVA that drives pigmentation. Photoprotection is routine architecture — not a summer add-on. <a href="/pages/daily-spf">Daily SPF literacy</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why a four-filter system?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Broader UVA1/UVA2/UVB coverage than many two-filter daily SPFs. Tinosorb S is included for modern, photostable UVA defence. <a href="/pages/ingredients#ingredient-tinosorb-s">Read Tinosorb S</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will it feel greasy on oily skin?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>It is built as a wearable aqua-gel with Zinc PCA at 0.5% to help sebum stay controlled in heat and humidity — because unused SPF is zero SPF.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How much should I apply?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Be generous as the last morning step. Reapply after heavy sweating or long outdoor exposure. Pair with barrier-aware moisturiser underneath so the film sits clean.</p></div>
    </details>

  {% when 'clear-seal' %}
    <details open>
      <summary>How is this different from a hydrocolloid patch?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>It is a liquid that dries to an invisible film while BHA, AHA, and Niacinamide treat the lesion — shielding from dirt and picking without bulk.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I use it with the full routine?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Yes, spot-wise on clean skin. Keep the rest of cleanse → treat → moisturise → protect consistent around it.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will it dry out my skin?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Acne treatments can dry; this formula includes a moisture-locking complex. Moisturise around the spot if the area feels tight.</p></div>
    </details>

  {% when 'active-boba-encapsulated-cream-acne-prone-skin' %}
    <details open>
      <summary>Why encapsulate the actives?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Treatment actives stay separated until application — supporting stability and fresher delivery versus a single-phase cream that ages on the shelf.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is this a moisturiser or a treatment?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Both roles by design: congestion and tone actives with ceramide barrier support so acne care does not abandon the lipid layer. <a href="/pages/acne">Acne literacy</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I introduce it?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>After cleanse, as directed on pack. If your barrier is reactive, start a few nights a week and keep SPF daily.</p></div>
    </details>

  {% when 'project-skin-complete-4-step-skincare-routine-kit' %}
    <details open>
      <summary>Why a kit instead of one “hero” product?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Acne-prone skin needs a sequence: clear without strip, treat oil pathways, repair lipids, protect from Indian UV. One serum cannot replace that architecture.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What order do I use the products?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Morning: Cleanse → Serum → Moisturiser → SPF. Evening: Cleanse → Serum → Moisturiser. Stay consistent before judging results.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I buy steps separately later?<span>+</span></summary>
      <div><p>Yes. Each formula is available individually once you know which step your skin relies on most.</p></div>
    </details>
{% endcase %}
